r's biological sex \"without written authorization from the pupil’s parent or legal guardian\". That requires permission, which is more than notice, so it matches rung 5 and rules out rung 4.\n- **Roll call:** Wichgers voted Aye (`Y WICHGERS R`) on a 50-43 vote. That is not near-unanimous.\n- **Bill history:** \"Representative Wichgers added as a coauthor\" on 3/11/2025. He joined before Assembly Amendment 1 was adopted, so his sponsorship covers the bill as filed.\n\n**Also coded, but they can't carry a chair on their own:**\n- **AB 963 (2021):** Aye, 60-34.\n- **AB 510 (2023):** coauthor, and Aye, 62-35.\n\nBoth are parental-rights bills covering many unrelated things, and their names clause only declares a right to \"determine the names and pronouns used for the child\". They lean the same way as AB 103 but don't establish a rung.\n\n**`needs_source`:** the text of Assembly Amendment 1 or the enrolled bill. That would confirm the written-authorization clause survived the amendment he voted on.\n\nThere are no quotes in his own words in the sources, so `quotes` is empty.","ttft_ms":24672,"type":"result","duration_ms":50594,"uuid":"a1805a04-d2d9-4da7-bc79-fb15385730be","ttft_stream_ms":1542,"time_to_request_ms":205,"first_content_frame_ms":1543,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
